ithout a garbage collector, what moves, copies and borrows mean, and how to read and fix the compiler's errors."],[35,"Add git packages with drachm add, version ranges, the lock file, deps/, several versions side by side, and packages that wrap C libraries."],[37,"An interactive window in safe Drachm over the SDL3 C library, with the unsafe part kept in one wrapper module."],[49,"Array and list types, literals, indexing with bounds checks, changing a list, its methods, comparing, for loops, splitting strings into lists, and maps with their keys, updates and walks. Parts still to come are marked."],[64,"Arrays, lists and maps as designed, the settings that will change lookups, and the parts still to come."],[65,"Borrow parameters, lend, lives on functions and structs, open and destroy."],[2,"Build the Drachm compiler and run, build and check a program."],[58,"build, run, check and explain, the -O flag, and exit codes."],[15,"Building structs with constructors, new ... of, fill blocks and def defaults."],[41,"Built-in types, bindings, number literals, conversions, operators and the text of values."],[27,"Characters versus bytes, string methods, interpolation and formatting, matching and looping over text, and reading input."],[10,"Choosing between many values with match, ranges and lists in cases, exhaustiveness warnings, and leaving if blocks with skip."],[28,"Choosing by value with match, from numbers and text to enums with guards and nesting, and when match beats an if chain."],[48,"Declaring enums, making values, matching with bindings, guards and nested patterns, exhaustiveness, equality, and how enums move and copy."],[42,"Declaring units, the SI set, numbers with units, arithmetic and conversion, points and deltas."],[31,"Designing a struct from its fields and methods to how its values are built, with constructors, fill blocks and defs."],[72,"drachm fmt, the Agora package registry, the language server and the standard library."],[68,"drachm.toml, dependencies,